{"repositoryId":33396684,"availability":"available","full":"mjskay/tidybayes","name":"tidybayes","description":"Bayesian analysis + tidy data + geoms (R package)","category":"Other","language":"R","stars":748,"forks":63,"created":"2015-04-04T06:35:31Z","updated":"2024-09-17T17:23:15Z","license":"GPL-3.0","branch":"master","homepage":"http://mjskay.github.io/tidybayes","topics":["bayesian-data-analysis","brms","ggplot2","jags","r","r-package","stan","tidy-data","visualization"],"demo":"http://mjskay.github.io/tidybayes","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:42.122Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:42.122Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:42.122Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T13:37:42.122Z","stars":748,"forks":63}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["tidybayes is an R package that aims to make it easy to integrate popular Bayesian modeling methods into a tidy data + ggplot workflow. It builds on top of (and re-exports) several functions for visualizing uncertainty from its sister package, ggdist","Tidy data frames (one observation per row) are particularly convenient for use in a variety of R data manipulation and visualization packages. However, when using Bayesian modeling functions like JAGS or Stan in R, we often have to translate this data into a form the model understands, and then after running the model, translate the resulting sample (or predictions) into a more tidy format for use with other R functions. tidybayes aims to simplify these two common (often tedious) operations:","translating data from a data.frame into a list , making sure factors are encoded as numerical data, adding variables to store the length of indices, etc. This package helps automate these operations using the composedata() function, which automatically handles data types like numeric, logical, factor, and ordinal, and allows easy extensions for converting other data types into a format the model understands by providing your own implementation of the generic asdatalist()."],"features":["Composing data for use with the model. This often means","Extracting tidy draws from the model. This often means extracting","Extracting tidy fits and predictions from models. For models like","Summarizing posterior distributions from models. tidybayes","Visualizing priors and posteriors. The focus on tidy data makes"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mjskay/tidybayes/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"7cd8ea0bff2868e3ff5e27e584e50d4647e48adb82fdbed90b422250c6e62cc1","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:42.269Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:42.269Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"tidybayes is an R package that aims to make it easy to integrate popular Bayesian modeling methods into a tidy data + ggplot workflow. It builds on top of (and re-exports) several functions for visualizing uncertainty from its sister package, ggdist","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mjskay/tidybayes/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"7cd8ea0bff2868e3ff5e27e584e50d4647e48adb82fdbed90b422250c6e62cc1","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mjskay/tidybayes/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:42.270Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2024-09-17T17:23:15Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/mjskay/tidybayes/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:42.272Z","hash":"7cd8ea0bff2868e3ff5e27e584e50d4647e48adb82fdbed90b422250c6e62cc1","originalBytes":28167,"storedBytes":28167,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["condition","data","draws","mean","tidybayes","ggdist","tidy","model","posterior","stat","functions","point","median","aes","geom","add","names","response","intervals","spread","ggplot","models","plot","library","mpg","width","broom","other","plots","epred","interval","like","mtcars","package","using","which","family","format","frames","types","abc","bayes","easy","fit","generate","means","prediction","pr